---
title: Exercise packs
---

An exercise pack adds a list of exercises to the catalogue. It's pure JSON — no
code, no sandbox — so it installs regardless of Restricted Mode.

## The fast path: export from the app

You don't have to write anything. In the app: **Exercises → long-press a custom
exercise → select a few → Export as pack**. You get a self-contained
`<name>.logit-pack.json` file that anyone can install from **Plugins → Add →
File**.

To publish it in a registry, split it into a manifest + data file (below), or
keep it inline.

## The pack file

```json
{
  "formatVersion": 1,
  "pluginId": "com.you.my-pack",
  "exercises": [
    {
      "name": "Zercher Squat",
      "primaryMuscles": ["quads"],
      "secondaryMuscles": ["core", "glutes"],
      "exerciseType": "normal"
    },
    {
      "name": "Nordic Hamstring Curl",
      "primaryMuscles": ["hamstrings"],
      "secondaryMuscles": ["calves"],
      "exerciseType": "bodyweight"
    }
  ]
}
```

- **Muscle groups** must be from: `chest`, `back`, `shoulders`, `biceps`,
  `triceps`, `quads`, `hamstrings`, `glutes`, `calves`, `core`, `forearms`.
- **`exerciseType`** (optional): `normal`, `assisted`, or `bodyweight`.
- Max 500 exercises. In-pack duplicate names are dropped.

## The manifest

```json
{
  "id": "com.you.my-pack",
  "family": "exercise-pack",
  "name": "My Pack",
  "description": "A few odd-lift movements.",
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "author": "You",
  "integrity": "sha256-…",
  "distribution": {
    "origin": "url",
    "manifestUrl": "plugins/my-pack/manifest.json",
    "bundleUrl": "plugins/my-pack/exercises.json"
  },
  "capabilities": [
    { "family": "exercise-pack", "exercisePackId": "com.you.my-pack" }
  ]
}
```

`capabilities[0].exercisePackId` must equal the manifest `id`.

## What happens on install

Pack exercises appear in the catalogue with namespaced ids
(`pack:<id>:<slug>`). A core or user exercise with the same name always wins.
Disabling or uninstalling the pack removes them cleanly. Pack contents are
device-local — they are not synced to your account.

Next: [publishing](/docs/plugins/publishing).
